      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SIMPLY ROSSO (4) is the horse to beat after a sound Carnarvon fourth where he raced wide throughout and was beaten just over a length. His previous 1000m win in a BM64, beating Kote by a long neck, gives him the right form line, and the slight rise in trip is no issue with no weight on his back. PRINCE RAGNAR (1) is the clear danger, coming off a third at Carnarvon and bringing an excellent Geraldton track-and-trip record. The inside draw is a big tick and Johnson's claim is a bonus as he'll be hard to run down from the front. ONEMORETWOMANY (2) resumes after eight months after disappointing before the break. His prior Geraldton win in BM70 over this track and trip rates highly though and that brings him right into calculations. SNIPPY SEAN (8) drops out of Ascot company and has had two trials. Easier here than what he's been racing in and he can return to form. GOLD KEEPER (3) has trialled well coming in and he can fire a shot on resumption.",
